<div class="tldr"><p><strong>Short answer:</strong> regular means you ride with your left foot forward; goofy means your right foot is forward. Neither is better. The right stance is simply the one that feels natural, and most people can find theirs in a minute with a couple of quick tests.</p></div>

<h2>What goofy and regular mean</h2>
<p>On a snowboard, one foot leads down the hill and the other stays at the back. Your front foot does most of the steering and carries a little more weight; your back foot pivots and pushes the tail around. Riders who lead with the left foot are <strong>regular</strong>. Riders who lead with the right foot are <strong>goofy</strong>. The names come from surfing and skateboarding, where the same stances exist.</p>
<p>There's no performance difference between the two. What matters is that your stance matches your body, because riding with the wrong foot forward makes every turn feel awkward.</p>

<table>
